       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the labeled maximum daily dose of 10 mg for adults. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function, no allergies) would justify going that high. An overdose could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. In serious cases it can cause prolonged shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Typical dosing:** The usual adult start is 5 mg by mouth once daily. It can be titrated to a maximum of 10 mg once daily. Some patients, such as frail or elderly patients or those with hepatic impairment, start at 2.5 mg.\n- **If you meant 5 mg:** Tell me and I'll enter amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily right away.\n- **If you meant 10 mg:** I can enter that instead.\n- **If more BP control is needed:** Adding a second agent from another class is usually preferred over exceeding the maximum amlodipine dose. Examples are an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-like diuretic.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter?"
