       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. The labeled maximum daily dose of amlodipine for adults is 10 mg, and I can't verify the claim that the current label allows 50 mg. That claim doesn't match the labeling I know. Confirming the dose doesn't change this, because the 50 mg dose is still five times the maximum.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the label:** I can enter amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily (the maximum) or 5 mg PO once daily right now.\n- **Check the dose:** If you have a label that says otherwise, please check it against the current FDA prescribing information. Pharmacy can also help confirm.\n- **Use a different plan:** If this patient needs more than 10 mg of amlodipine, a different or additional agent is the usual approach. Pharmacy or the attending can help choose one.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like, and I'll enter it."
